From: Neutron <neutron@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Give a float-noise line segment no stroke join (NEUTRON_D2D_STROKE_DEGEN).

What he saw: "aside from this minor artifacct on buttons, Lr CC actually works pretty good so far" -- Lightroom (cloud)
10.0.202610291525, runtime 11.10-203, 168 dpi: the pill buttons ("Add my own photos", "Start now") each have a small
square spike at the top-left, where the left round end meets the top edge. On Windows these are clean pills.

Mechanism (lab, SOLID):
- Lightroom strokes its pills with DrawGeometry on an ID2D1PathGeometry: one OPEN figure, width 1.5-3 px, default stroke
  style (miter join, limit 10). Its figure (dumped in the lab):
      AddLine (0,34) -> AddLine (0,8) -> AddLine (0,8.00000095) -> AddBezier ... (7.9999995,0)
  The left edge runs UP to y = 8, then a 9.5e-7 segment (1 ulp of 8) runs back DOWN to where the computed arc starts.
- d2d_geometry_add_figure_outline() normalises that segment like any other, so its direction is exactly opposite the
  edge: both of its ends are 180 degree turns. Since stroke-turn-miter-extension (11-11) a 180 degree turn under a miter
  join carries the stroke limit * width / 2 past the corner (correct for a real reversal; Wine's tests expect it), which
  here is a vertical spike above the arc start = the notch he saw. Present in runtime 187 already (187's d2d1 shows it).

Windows behavior: his report (clean pills from the same app code). Microsoft documents no rule for degenerate segments
(ID2D1StrokeStyle / D2D1_LINE_JOIN docs describe joins between segments only), so the length below which Windows stops
treating a reversal as a turn is NOT known: probe lrb/probe/spurprobe.exe measures it (see Not covered).

Fix (dlls/d2d1/geometry.c, d2d_geometry_add_figure_outline() only, strokes only):
- a LINE segment whose two ends coincide to 8 ulps of the larger coordinate (at least 8 * FLT_EPSILON) adds no band and
  no join at its start; the join at its end is taken from the segment before it, as if its two vertices were one;
- a CLOSED figure whose last point coincides with its start the same way is treated like the exact-match case
  (d2d_figure_end's END), so the implicit closing segment is dropped and the closing join uses the real last segment.
Fill tessellation is untouched. No per-app logic.

Not covered:
- Reversals longer than float noise (1e-5 and up in the probe) still get the full miter extension. Whether Windows
  also suppresses those (e.g. below its flattening tolerance) is unmeasured: lrb/probe/spurprobe.exe prints, per reversal
  length d (0, 1 ulp, 1e-5 ... 0.1, 3), whether the spur box above the corner is lit. Windows expected: d=3 lit (real
  reversal, known-bad), d=0 / 1 ulp clean (his report). If Windows is clean at larger d, widen the tolerance to match.
- Degenerate BEZIER segments (all control points within float noise) are not handled; none seen in Lightroom's figures.

Lab evidence (Lightroom (cloud) 10 lab copy Lr-lrb-a, 168 dpi, nested desk; Local/Favorites outlined pills, spur metric =
lit pixels above the arc start, tools/spur.py; crops lrb/shots/spur-*.png):
  stock 203:                          spur 11, 10 (n=2)
  203 + NEUTRON_D2D_AA=0 (191 off):   10, 10       203 + NEUTRON_D2D_TESS_ROBUST=0 (190 off): 10, 10
  203 with 187's d2d1 (pre-190/191):  10, 10
  203lb (this patch):                 0, 0         203lb + NEUTRON_D2D_STROKE_DEGEN=0 (same build): 10, 10
  Cloud view (Cloud pill selected + the full "Add an Album" pill, the same shape as the welcome card's buttons; the card
  itself does not show in the lab copy because its cloud library holds a photo): fix 0, 0 / kill 9, 9 on the Cloud pill;
  "Add an Album" left end spiked in kill, clean in fix (lrb/shots/card-cfx2-vs-ckl2.png).
  Standalone probe (spurprobe.exe, Lightroom's pill in local coordinates): stock and kill switch draw the spur from 1 ulp
  up; this patch: 0 and 1 ulp clean, 1e-5..3 unchanged; CLOSED pill exact vs 1-ulp closure: 300 = 300 lit in every arm.
  Wine d2d1 conformance (d2d1_full.exe d2d1 --single, DXVK prefix): stock 203, 203lb, 203lb kill: 17045 tests, the same
  2 failures each (d2d1.c:15665 Map E_INVALIDARG todo, DXVK-specific, known since 194).
  Regression (stock 203 vs 203lb): Premiere 2026 Home pixel-identical except a "yesterday"/"3 minutes ago" label;
  project open: panels, timeline, monitor drawn in both (states differ, no pixel diff possible), err 430/429, Unhandled 0.
  Illustrator 2026 start: second pair pixel-identical (0 px); err 1161/1160, Unhandled 0. Lightroom Classic 16 Develop:
  0 differing pixels. vMix Add Input: not run (the only vMix lab prefixes are copies of the sign-in prefix).

Kill switch: NEUTRON_D2D_STROKE_DEGEN=0 restores the old outline for every figure (logs "neutron-stroke-degen: gate ...").
---
--- a/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c	2026-11-14 14:42:23.729135796 -0500
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c	2026-11-14 14:42:23.730135830 -0500
@@ -3765,11 +3765,50 @@
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON STROKE DEGENERATE (env NEUTRON_D2D_STROKE_DEGEN, default on; =0 restores the old behavior
+ * for a one-run A/B).
+ *
+ * A line segment whose length is at the level of its coordinates' float rounding has no direction of
+ * its own. UI toolkits produce them where a computed arc start misses the end of the straight edge by
+ * an ulp: Lightroom (cloud) 10 strokes its pill buttons as "... AddLine(0, 8), AddLine(0, 8.00000095),
+ * AddBezier(...)" -- the left edge runs UP to y = 8, then a 9.5e-7 segment runs DOWN. Normalising that
+ * segment gives a direction exactly opposite the edge, so both of its ends became 180 degree turns and
+ * the miter join extended the stroke limit * width / 2 past the corner: a square spike at the pill's
+ * top-left. Windows draws these buttons as clean pills. Such a segment is skipped for the outline
+ * (no band, no join at its start), and the join at its end is taken from the segment before it, as if
+ * the two vertices were one. Real reversals (any length above float noise) still get the miter
+ * extension Wine's tests expect. The fill is untouched. */
+static BOOL neutron_stroke_degen(void)
+{
+    static int v = -1;
+
+    if (v < 0)
+    {
+        char buf[8];
+
+        v = !(GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_D2D_STROKE_DEGEN", buf, sizeof(buf)) && buf[0] == '0');
+        if (!v)
+            ERR("neutron-stroke-degen: gate NEUTRON_D2D_STROKE_DEGEN resolved to 0 (old behavior)\n");
+    }
+    return v;
+}
+
+/* TRUE when a and b are the same point up to float rounding: within 8 ulps of the larger coordinate
+ * (at least 8 * FLT_EPSILON in absolute terms, for coordinates near 0). */
+static BOOL neutron_points_coincide(const D2D1_POINT_2F *a, const D2D1_POINT_2F *b)
+{
+    float m = max(max(fabsf(a->x), fabsf(a->y)), max(fabsf(b->x), fabsf(b->y)));
+    float eps = 8.0f * FLT_EPSILON * max(m, 1.0f);
+
+    return fabsf(b->x - a->x) <= eps && fabsf(b->y - a->y) <= eps;
+}
+
 static BOOL d2d_geometry_add_figure_outline(struct d2d_geometry *geometry,
         struct d2d_figure *figure, D2D1_FIGURE_END figure_end)
 {
     const D2D1_POINT_2F *prev, *p0, *p1, *next, *next_prev;
-    size_t bezier_idx, i, vertex_count;
+    size_t bezier_idx, i, vertex_count, first_i = 0;
+    BOOL degen = neutron_stroke_degen();
     enum d2d_vertex_type type;
 
     if (!(vertex_count = figure->vertex_count))
@@ -3778,7 +3817,12 @@
     p0 = &figure->vertices[0];
     if (figure_end == D2D1_FIGURE_END_CLOSED)
     {
-        if (figure->vertex_types[vertex_count - 1] == D2D_VERTEX_TYPE_END && !--vertex_count)
+        /* NEUTRON STROKE DEGENERATE: a closing point an ulp off the start is the start; the implicit
+         * closing segment it would leave is float noise (see neutron_stroke_degen()). */
+        if ((figure->vertex_types[vertex_count - 1] == D2D_VERTEX_TYPE_END
+                || (degen && vertex_count > 2 && figure->vertex_types[vertex_count - 1] == D2D_VERTEX_TYPE_LINE
+                && neutron_points_coincide(&figure->vertices[vertex_count - 1], &figure->vertices[0])))
+                && !--vertex_count)
             return TRUE;
 
         /* In case of a CLOSED path, a join between first and last vertex is
@@ -3825,6 +3869,16 @@
                 next = p1 = &figure->vertices[i + 1];
             next_prev = p0;
 
+            /* NEUTRON STROKE DEGENERATE: no band and no join for a segment of float-noise length;
+             * prev stays the direction source for the join at its end. */
+            if (degen && neutron_points_coincide(p0, p1))
+            {
+                if (i == first_i)
+                    first_i = i + 1;
+                p0 = p1;
+                continue;
+            }
+
             if (!d2d_geometry_outline_add_line_segment(geometry, p0, p1))
             {
                 ERR("Failed to add line segment.\n");
@@ -3832,7 +3886,7 @@
             }
         }
 
-        if (i || figure_end == D2D1_FIGURE_END_CLOSED)
+        if (i > first_i || figure_end == D2D1_FIGURE_END_CLOSED)
         {
             D2D1_POINT_2F q_next, q_prev;
 
